# Tandem Cross-Agent Code Review (`tandem-cross-agent-code-review`)

Having two state-of-the-art reasoning models running simultaneously enables continuous peer review. Before merging feature branches (`feat/argon-work` or `feat/fable-work`) back to `main`, each model conducts an automated peer audit on the other's code.

---

## 1. Review Matrix & Division of Strengths

| Model Conducting Review | Target Code Under Review | Review Focus | Key Strengths Leveraged |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Argon Audits Fable** | C++ 64-bit diffs, Engine memory allocators | Architectural soundness, memory leaks, boundary conditions, edge cases | Deep deliberative reasoning, SentencePiece density |
| **Fable Audits Argon** | LTX configs, Lua scripts, Shader declarations | Syntax precision, AST compliance, missing brackets, parameter typos | High token density, strict linting gates, surgical diff checks |

---

## 2. Peer Review Workflow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Argon (Pane 0)
    participant S as .agents/handoff.json
    participant F as Fable (Pane 1)
    
    F->>S: 1. Post C++ diff to .agents/handoff.json (Status: Review_Requested)
    A->>S: 2. Read diff; perform adversarial self-critique
    A->>S: 3. Post Approval or Surgical Suggestions
    F->>F: 4. Apply suggestions & proceed to clean merge
```

---

## 3. High-Density Review Template

Peer reviews must be compact (< 20 lines) to avoid context bloat:

```text
[PEER_AUDIT from Argon to Fable]
- Target: xrGame/weapon_ak74.cpp#L214
- Status: APPROVED with 1 warning
- Note: Casting to uint32_t on line 214 truncates 64-bit pointers on OGSR Linux; replace with uintptr_t.
```
